{
  "doc": "The Home Assistant integration's contract with Logger (logger_app, github.com/sgtpepperpt/ha-logger-app; docs/home-assistant.md): one example answer of every route it reads — GET /about, GET /status?tz=, GET /quick (one entry of each kind), POST /quick/<id>/fire (201, and a med tick's 409 with `already`), POST /shopping (201, and 202 = queued while Nextcloud is down), POST /tablet/wake (200, and 409 = not set up), GET /alerts — keyed by HTTP status where a route has two. Rules + scenes (F39, `about.features` has \"rules\"): `ha_catalog.request` = the body the integration PUTs to /ha/catalog (Logger checks it is accepted), `ha_actions` = GET /ha/actions (the integration's every poll: waiting actions to run + the revs it refetches /ha/rules?kind=from_ha and /ha/scenes on), `ha_action_result` = POST /ha/actions/<id>/result, `ha_rules` = GET /ha/rules?kind=from_ha (HA-side triggers to register; a `device` one carries the trigger config as HA listed it), `ha_rule_fire` = POST /ha/rules/<id>/fire (an HA trigger happened: Logger runs the rule's Logger-side actions itself), `ha_rule_state` = POST /ha/rules/<id>/state (registration outcome), `ha_scenes` = GET /ha/scenes, `ha_webhook` = the body Logger POSTs to the integration's webhook (a nudge, never data). backend/tests/test_ha_contract.py checks every key path here against what the server answers, with the same JSON type (null = the key is nullable); the integration's tests parse a copy. A key the server adds never breaks the integration and never bumps `about.api`; a key it reads renamed, removed or retyped does both. `status.food` = status_parity.json's first case (25 Oct 13:30Z, Lisbon). `status.changes` is keyed by data: one key per kind written so far (food, body, blood, journal, meds, goals, pressure, workouts, tasks). Null means unknown, never 0: no calorie goal, no medication today, Tasks off. A Daily care slot an entry ticked (F67: a reading, a body entry, a workout… the item is done by) is answered and leaves `care`; one whose item asks to review it stays owed and carries `evidence` {kind, at, words, what, id}, the entry it offers as its tick (null on every other slot). Calendar (F74, `about.features` has \"calendar\"): `status.calendar` = the next event and today’s (status_parity.json’s calendar case at 5 Nov 14:00, Lisbon: `next` the first still to start — a timed one up to 10 min after its start, an all-day one from its first day after today — with `in_min`; `rows` today’s occurrences, all-day first, ended ones too; `today_n` all of today’s; null while Calendar is off), `calendar_events` = GET /calendar/events?from&to&tz (the occurrences overlapping [from, to) in `instances`, each event once in `events`, keyed by its id; an all-day occurrence’s days in `start_date` … `end_date`, exclusive). Instants are ISO 8601 with an offset; the caller's `tz` decides every day. Every id and address is made up: the instance a v4 UUID of zeros, the HA device id a counting pattern, the trigger id a made-up one (the integration's own are `trigger_id()` of the config), the webhook on a documentation address (192.0.2.0/24). `about.version` = the release (the repo's VERSION, SemVer), added with F70: null from a server that can't say. Voice (F69, `about.features` has \"voice\"): `command_vocab` = GET /command/vocab?tz (the words the integration builds Assist’s sentences from; `units` = the portion types those foods are said in), `command_parse` = GET /command/parse?text&tz (a reading, nothing written: `eager` = sure enough to write, else `needs` or `warning` say why not; `alternatives` the other readings: the integration keeps the first of the kind its sentence asked for), `command_run` = POST /command/run (`request` = the body the integration sends, `source: voice`; 201, and 400 with `needs`), `voice.sentences` = what speech-to-text gives (`said`, `lang`), the sentence family the integration’s sentences match it to, the line it sends (`text`) and the intent Logger reads it as, eagerly: the integration checks its sentences over `command_vocab`, Logger its grammar over test_command’s world (tests/test_ha_voice.py).",
  "errors": "A refusal is always JSON with `error` = the words to show; a route's own may add keys (`ok`, `already`, `field`); the server's own are exactly {\"error\": <words>, \"status\": <code>}: an unknown route 404 \"Nothing at that address.\", a wrong method 405, a body that is no JSON 400 (not sent as JSON 415), a server fault 500 \"Something broke on the server · ref <id>\". An answer that is not JSON is a proxy's, never Logger's.",
